<title>JAPAN: UK inflation likely to be below 2.5% target--BOE.</title>
<headline>UK inflation likely to be below 2.5% target--BOE.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's inflation rate is likely to fall below the government's target of 2.5 percent this year, Howard Davies, deputy governor of the Bank of England, said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;As far as the short term is concerned, inflation will likely fall below 2.5 percent within the current year at current exchange rates,&quot; Davies said in reply to questions after a speech to the Federation of Bankers' Associations of Japan in Tokyo.</p>
</text>
